    "causalModel": {
      "founding": "An adult wamasu grew into a small isolated pan of standing water beside the zone's poling line and has held it for years.",
      "siteAdvantages": "The one closed body of still water within 300 m: fed by the water table, cut off from the tidal channels and shallow enough that the animal can stand in all of it. A low bank ring, one knoll above it and a cave mouth at the west waterline that floods to the roof.",
      "occupantsMotive": "The animal holds ground that it can charge; the villages have stopped trying to take it back and now leave offerings on the south bank in the old Shadowfen manner.",
      "pressures": "The poling detour costs two hours and runs within 30 m of the pond for its whole length; the pole line needs patching every season.",
      "wouldChangeIf": "Killing the animal reopens the direct line and ends the offerings; the tribes disagree about whether that is a gain."
